WEBVTT

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:10.270
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:20.040
Rental Magica

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:28.120
The shadow of the moon as it waxes and wanes...
Michikakeru tsuki no kage sotto

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:37.800
...gently stirs the beat of sorrow in your heart.
kanashimi no kodou furuwasu

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:42.490
Its wandering attraction...
Samayou inryoku

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.430
...reflected in your eyes.
hitomi ni utsushite

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.420
You will surpass the darkness of Ioneliness.
Kodoku no yami wo koeteyuku

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:59.120
You know that truth in your heart.
Shinjitsu wa kono mune ni

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:04.790
That gentleness will become your strength.
Yasashisa wa tsuyosa ni naru

00:01:04.790 --> 00:01:09.430
Don't be afraid. Believe.
Osorenaide shinjiru koto

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:14.270
The brilliance that blooms in the cosmos eternally...
Sora ni saku kirameki wa towa ni

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.240
...embraces the voice of time.
toki no koe dakishime

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:24.310
Play your dream for me.
Kanadete yume

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.050
Let me hear.
Kikasete

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:33.780
Wind, speak to me.
Kaze tsutaete

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:40.290
Tell me what courage is.
Yuuki wo

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.330
This feels great!

00:01:49.070 --> 00:01:50.000
Itsuki.

00:01:51.870 --> 00:01:53.100
Would you like some herbal tea?

00:01:54.680 --> 00:01:55.640
Thanks.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:00.580
Do I look bad in it?

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.180
I looked at lots of magazines...

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.150
...and asked Honami for her advice,
then chose this one.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.490
N-No! It looks great on you.

00:02:10.490 --> 00:02:11.620
Oh, I'm glad!

00:02:12.060 --> 00:02:17.560
Um, that herbal tea's the usual,
except I added hibiscus and rose hips.

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:19.870
It tastes great!

00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:21.030
Wow!

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.700
The sea!

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.100
Ow! Ow! Hot! Hot!

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:32.040
Mikan!

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.410
Hot! Hot! Hot!

00:02:34.850 --> 00:02:36.450
Oh, for crying out loud.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.180
You promised you'd wait till
everyone was here, didn't you?

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:42.320
But how often do we go
on company trips like this?

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:45.350
The ocean's so pretty! I just have to play in it!

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:48.320
Right, right, just put on your sandals, first.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:51.000
Oh, those are so lame.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:51.730
What are you talking about?

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:55.290
I never knew Japan had such pretty beaches.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.560
What's wrong, Itsuki?

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.410
You see something you like?

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.450
Um, well, that is...

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:07.810
Addie, why do you always
show up in these situations?!

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.780
And what's the deal with that bathing suit?!

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:13.520
I can have one made for you, if you like.

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:19.390
Although, we might have
to take it in a bit to fit you.

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.020
Say what?!

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.200
You two, we didn't come all
this way so you could fight...

00:03:25.300 --> 00:03:26.460
I challenge you on this beach!

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.930
Just what I was hoping!

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:30.570
Guys, like I just said...

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.830
Nekoyashiki, thank goodness you're here.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.200
Please, stop them...

00:03:36.510 --> 00:03:38.570
Careful guys, it's hot.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.720
Behold, the spirit!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:51.720
The humble simplicity! Let's bushido!

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.330
Like the pads of a cat's foot,

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.390
the fundoshi has been spoken
of since time immemorial!

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.630
Something that no true son
of Japan should be without!

00:04:08.410 --> 00:04:12.540
Itsuki and the others must be
having fun at the beach now.

00:04:13.050 --> 00:04:17.210
Probably. Although we did give them
that little task to perform, too.

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.250
The funadama, huh?

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:26.090
Episode 15
LEGEND OF THE MERMAID

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:38.000
Hey there, barefoot mermaids.

00:04:38.270 --> 00:04:39.370
Wanna hang with us?

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:44.370
Do your best, both of you!

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:47.470
Brother Pres, keep the right score, okay?

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:48.780
R-Right.

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.790
I'm training for the Straits of Gibraltar!

00:04:52.890 --> 00:04:55.080
And I'm training for the Akashi Strait!

00:04:55.720 --> 00:04:56.750
I'm not losing to you!

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:58.020
Same goes for me!

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:00.130
You don't know when to quit!

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:01.690
Neither do you!

00:05:01.930 --> 00:05:03.790
Go! Go!

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:10.140
That's what you get for overdoing it.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:11.230
Are you okay?

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:36.560
You never change, Itsuki.

00:05:37.130 --> 00:05:39.030
You think pirate ghosts will jump out at you?

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:42.130
I... I told you not to say that!

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:52.640
Be careful.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:55.580
That doll is called a funadama.

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:01.460
It's a charm dating from Meiji-period
Edo that was used by many ships...

00:06:01.460 --> 00:06:02.950
...to pray for safe voyages.

00:06:04.390 --> 00:06:07.520
It apparently washed up on the beach.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.300
The person who found it
saw that it was very old...

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:17.470
and that it seemed to be cursed, so they
couldn't throw it away. They brought it to us.

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.980
I'm sorry, but can you return
this to where it came from?

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:25.910
The place is...

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:31.850
I'm glad.

00:06:32.150 --> 00:06:33.920
Hm? Did you say something?

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:36.550
No, it's nothing.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:43.030
What the?!

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:51.340
Itsuki!

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:05.240
Huh? The president and Kuroha...

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:06.420
Where did they go?

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:09.720
They went to return the funadama, but...

00:07:10.060 --> 00:07:12.530
It's weird. They haven't come back yet.

00:07:12.890 --> 00:07:16.800
Actually, I've been keeping
in contact with Byakko,

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:20.830
but for some reason,
there's no response at all from him now.

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:29.340
Itsuki! Itsuki! Itsuki!

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:31.900
Thank goodness.

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:39.180
Huh?!

00:07:39.720 --> 00:07:40.740
We're at sea?!

00:07:40.990 --> 00:07:42.390
You awake, kid?

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:43.680
Who are you?

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.650
Oh, you're livelier than I'd expect.

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:52.230
When I spotted you drifting with
that cat, I thought you'd drowned.

00:07:54.600 --> 00:07:55.590
I'm Hyodo.

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:59.200
Itsuki Iba. Um, where am I?

00:07:59.570 --> 00:08:01.670
That's what I'd like to know.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:06.040
I was out fishing three days ago
and got caught in this weird fog.

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:08.970
I haven't been able to get out of it since.

00:08:09.720 --> 00:08:11.620
Also, take a look at that.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:17.480
There are all sorts of ships I've never
seen before drifting around here.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.890
I'd ask for help,

00:08:19.890 --> 00:08:23.090
but I don't want to get anywhere
near those creepy-looking ships.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:25.730
Yeah, right.

00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:27.670
I think you should keep away, too.

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:37.180
Nekoyashiki, come in! Nekoyashiki!

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:43.010
Itsuki! I tried to fly out, but...

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:45.810
I just suddenly found myself back here.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:47.980
No good on my end, either.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:52.130
Byakko is an agathion, so he should be able
to share his five senses with Nekoyashiki...

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:54.530
...no matter how far away he is, but...

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.060
Where can we be?

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:01.560
Besides that, there's this boat,
and Hyodo's clothes, too.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.900
The only explanation is that he's
from another time, isn't it?

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.770
So, you're saying this is?

00:09:07.010 --> 00:09:09.440
Yeah. I think it's spell wave contamination.

00:09:10.210 --> 00:09:12.180
Oh, what do we do?

00:09:12.780 --> 00:09:16.580
Theoretically, to destroy spell wave
contamination, you destroy the core.

00:09:17.390 --> 00:09:20.080
So, how do I find the core?

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.990
We're at sea! I can't do anything!

00:09:25.690 --> 00:09:28.530
Itsuki, calm down and think.

00:09:29.200 --> 00:09:31.100
There must be something that's causing this.

00:09:31.230 --> 00:09:32.160
But...

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.420
Mutsumi...

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:37.500
Mutsumi, I'll be home soon...

00:09:39.370 --> 00:09:41.100
For Hyodo's sake, too.

00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:42.670
You're right.

00:09:43.340 --> 00:09:47.180
Okay, let's try and remember
what we've learned up till now.

00:09:47.950 --> 00:09:52.850
Okay, there are a few different
kinds of spell wave contamination.

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:55.320
Recursion and endowment are close to this.

00:09:55.690 --> 00:10:00.630
Recursion has the effect of taking you back
to the past within the contaminated area,

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:05.630
but since people from different times like us
and Hyodo are in the same contamination zone,

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:06.860
that doesn't apply.

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:08.830
That leaves endowment.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.840
That applies to something
endowing magical properties...

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.710
...to objects and life forms
within the contaminated area.

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:21.840
In other words, the core of this spell wave
contamination is something to do with this boat.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.090
That's strange. They still haven't
put the funadama back.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.050
Besides that, do you feel that aura?

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:33.490
Something's weird about it.

00:10:34.930 --> 00:10:40.230
Could they have been caught up in some
type of spell wave contamination?

00:10:40.970 --> 00:10:43.030
The president, Kuroha, and Byakko...

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:48.310
How are those three going to be able
to break a spell wave contamination?

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.910
You people...

00:10:57.720 --> 00:10:59.450
Hyodo, um...

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.150
Why do you keep throwing away
the fish that you've caught?

00:11:03.590 --> 00:11:06.030
Because they're not what I'm after.

00:11:07.400 --> 00:11:09.330
So, what are you trying to catch?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:11.470
Why are you asking me that?!

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.960
Um, well...

00:11:13.100 --> 00:11:17.800
My work involves magic,
the occult and stuff like that, so...

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:18.700
Huh?

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.300
Um, like... Fortune telling and stuff like that.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.770
I might be able to find a way out of here.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:30.040
I was told never to tell this
to anyone but my successor.

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:34.990
My family's been sailing for
generations. My ancestors...

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.820
...caught mermaids.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:38.750
Mermaids?!

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:45.730
When I was a kid, I was fed the last piece of it.

00:11:46.570 --> 00:11:50.400
The lung infection I had was cured instantly.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.870
It was a first-rate medicine,

00:11:53.510 --> 00:11:55.630
and tasted better than anything I'd ever had.

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:57.870
I'll never forget that taste.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:10.580
Legends?

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:16.560
Right, do you know of any sort of strange
effects in this area or weird folktales?

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.500
Are you talking about the mermaids?

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.230
Mermaids?
Mermaids?

00:12:19.230 --> 00:12:21.130
It's a terrible legend.

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.430
It disgusts me to even speak of it.

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:27.800
They're not like the mermaids that show
up in the world of fairy tales, are they?

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:31.000
Grotesque creatures, neither human nor fish.

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:35.880
The legend of Yaobikuni says that eating
their flesh makes you immortal.

00:12:36.250 --> 00:12:41.520
I once saw a mummified mermaid handed
down at a shrine in the countryside.

00:12:41.520 --> 00:12:43.180
Go back to where you came from.

00:12:43.460 --> 00:12:47.290
The locals here rarely go near
this place even in the daytime.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.430
I came to warn you when I saw you go in here.

00:12:52.030 --> 00:12:53.200
Wait, please!

00:12:53.200 --> 00:12:56.360
Could you tell us a bit more about the legend?

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.300
We've lost contact with three of our friends.

00:13:00.840 --> 00:13:02.470
I ask you, as well.

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:06.140
"Beware the thick fog."

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:10.080
"One who has eaten the flesh of a mermaid..."

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.790
"...will eventually be devoured by them."

00:13:14.460 --> 00:13:18.050
It's an old tale passed down
by the local fishermen.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:22.530
I pray that your friends haven't
been swallowed up by it.

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:24.160
Icchan...

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:28.130
I hope he doesn't go meddling
where he shouldn't, but...

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:34.370
So, do you perform any unusual
rituals when you go fishing?

00:13:34.640 --> 00:13:38.280
When we make a boat or
pass it on to a successor,

00:13:38.280 --> 00:13:40.250
we always perform an elaborate rite.

00:13:40.780 --> 00:13:45.050
They said it was to pray that
we would catch a mermaid.

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:47.610
We'd paint the bottom of the boat with blood.

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.190
Funny, huh?

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:54.520
Mermaids, who are eaten by humans,
eat humans in return.

00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:56.330
And who is Mutsumi?

00:13:56.660 --> 00:13:59.030
Oh, was I talking in my sleep?

00:14:01.340 --> 00:14:02.670
My dead daughter.

00:14:04.410 --> 00:14:07.070
My daughter by the wife who left me,

00:14:07.940 --> 00:14:12.640
because I was out at sea when
my daughter took sick and died.

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:16.240
I couldn't tell if my home was
with my family or the sea,

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:19.650
and so my daughter died while I was away.

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:23.080
But you were trying to catch a
mermaid to save your daughter, right?

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.150
I still wasn't there for her while she was dying.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:32.100
I'm sorry for bringing up
such hard memories for you.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:34.670
No, it happened a long time ago.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:36.200
Look!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:45.240
Itsuki, over there!

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:51.180
You ate me, didn't you?

00:14:51.350 --> 00:14:52.720
Ate me, ate me...

00:14:52.720 --> 00:14:53.590
Mermaids!
Ate me, ate me...

00:14:53.590 --> 00:14:55.110
This time, I...

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.820
This time, I...

00:15:03.700 --> 00:15:05.760
...shall eat YOU!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:14.900
Kuroha!

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:24.370
Thick fog signals the coming of mermaids...

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.550
I didn't think the old legend was true!

00:15:26.550 --> 00:15:27.820
Is there no way out of this?!

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.360
It's no use.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.190
I... threw it away.

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:33.880
Threw what away?!

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:39.460
My ancestors would throw a doll into
the sea to act as a substitute for them.

00:15:40.100 --> 00:15:43.000
The doll was called a funadama.

00:15:44.240 --> 00:15:46.170
It was made by Mutsumi.

00:15:47.070 --> 00:15:51.530
I have no right to for her protection
when I couldn't protect her!

00:15:52.310 --> 00:15:54.870
That's why I threw it into
the sea before I came here.

00:15:55.550 --> 00:15:58.520
Even so, because I could do nothing else,

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:01.150
I've been searching for the
mermaids ever since.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:05.650
Give us the man! Give us the man!
Give us the man!

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:07.760
Heh, they're calling me.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:08.990
So long.

00:16:09.230 --> 00:16:12.060
Once I'm dead, I'm sure you'll
be able to get out of here.

00:16:12.170 --> 00:16:12.790
Wait!

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:21.640
Hyodo!

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:23.910
It's okay, he's just unconscious.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.640
Itsuki, leave this to me!

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:30.280
With that funadama,
I may be able to do something!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.920
I beg of you, Mutsumi!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:47.730
Mutsumi! Please, lend me your power!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:55.970
The wish you put into the funadama...

00:16:58.480 --> 00:16:59.880
Entrust it to me!

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:05.850
Kuroha!

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:07.350
It's all right.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:10.490
The feelings Mutusmi put into this doll...

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:12.250
Somehow, I understand them completely!

00:17:14.830 --> 00:17:18.630
A person's feelings can live on,
even after death.

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.130
I'll give form to Mutusmi's feelings!

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:26.670
Kuroha!

00:17:33.880 --> 00:17:34.940
Kuroha, what's wrong?!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.340
Kuroha, don't disappear!

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:41.680
I-I...

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:43.390
What's happening?

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:44.360
I don't know!

00:17:45.190 --> 00:17:46.090
Don't disappear!

00:17:46.390 --> 00:17:47.690
Don't disappear, Kuroha!

00:17:50.900 --> 00:17:53.200
That's... Mutsumi's!

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:55.930
Kuroha! Don't disappear!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:57.390
Itsuki...

00:17:57.970 --> 00:17:58.870
Why?

00:17:59.740 --> 00:18:01.710
Why is the doll here?!

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.410
It was Mutsumi, wasn't it?

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.680
She sent it to me.

00:18:11.350 --> 00:18:12.220
Thank you.

00:18:15.590 --> 00:18:17.350
Thank you, Mutsumi.

00:18:22.430 --> 00:18:24.900
He comes! He comes! Devour him! Devour him!

00:18:25.100 --> 00:18:26.730
Devour him! Devour him!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:47.980
Even now, Mutsumi still loves her father.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.350
So please, stop searching for the mermaids.

00:18:52.330 --> 00:18:53.990
Please go home.

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.290
To the home you shared with Mutsumi.

00:19:05.210 --> 00:19:06.570
Good job too, Byakko.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.630
Itsuki, your body...

00:19:08.910 --> 00:19:09.930
I get it.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:14.340
Kuroha was just being forced
out of this space first...

00:19:22.360 --> 00:19:24.690
Farewell, Hyodo.

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:35.060
So, they come back and we see this?

00:19:35.470 --> 00:19:36.490
For heaven's sake.

00:19:36.600 --> 00:19:37.700
Now, now...

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:48.410
Kuroha!

00:19:52.990 --> 00:19:54.780
Oh, I see.

00:19:56.120 --> 00:20:00.530
The sadness inhabiting the doll acted
in concert with the mermaid legend...

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.520
...when it was returned here.

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.820
It led the president and the
others to another world.

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:08.830
So, another unpaid job, huh? Great...

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:10.930
Yeah, I guess it turned out that way.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.770
Huh? Kuroha?

00:20:16.910 --> 00:20:18.840
Still, I'm glad.

00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:21.940
She seems happy now.

00:20:27.590 --> 00:20:28.750
Thank you.

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:33.350
Actually, I heard a wondrous thing at
a nearby shrine after it happened.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:34.890
A wondrous thing?

00:20:35.560 --> 00:20:37.790
That old shrine in the cave...

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:43.400
Some people connected with it showed up
and wanted to make a proper offering.

00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:47.000
Apparently, their ancestors have
been fishermen for generations.

00:20:49.580 --> 00:20:54.710
Now that the funadama has been returned,
they've realized that the shrine was theirs.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:20:58.840
Thank goodness.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:01.180
He made it back to the real world.

00:21:03.660 --> 00:21:05.680
That's why the funadama did all that!

00:21:05.790 --> 00:21:07.990
By the way, how'd the company trip go?

00:21:08.360 --> 00:21:10.990
I'll bet you were swimming in girls!

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:14.230
Um, you could say that...

00:21:20.140 --> 00:21:23.770
They don't have to look so scary
while lighting fireworks, do they?

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:25.050
Exactly.

00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:25.980
I agree.

00:21:30.850 --> 00:21:32.610
All right, I win!

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:33.890
What were you looking at?

00:21:33.890 --> 00:21:35.960
Mine clearly burned the longest.

00:21:35.960 --> 00:21:37.290
No, mine did!

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:38.380
Mine did!

00:21:38.460 --> 00:21:39.660
Mine did!

00:21:39.660 --> 00:21:40.330
Mine!

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:41.030
Mine!
Mine!

00:21:41.030 --> 00:21:41.720
Mine!

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:47.260
Fireworks!

00:21:58.250 --> 00:22:07.850
Over and over, holding my wounded hand...
Kizutsuku te wo nandomo tsunaide

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:16.250
...you walk this uncertain path with me...
fuan bakari no kono michi wo aruite

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:29.310
...amidst the days as they slowly drift by.
yukkuri nagareta hibi no naka de bokura ga

00:22:29.580 --> 00:22:41.220
The things we obtain are so warm, so beloved.
Te ni shita mono wa konna ni atatakute itoshinda

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:47.490
Please, as time goes by, let's keep right on...
Nee konomama toki no naka

00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:52.000
...laughing and walking together.
waratte aruite yukou

00:22:52.870 --> 00:22:56.270
It's because you're with me...
Kimi ga iru kara

00:22:56.270 --> 00:23:01.370
...that I can keep moving forward.
mae ni susumerunda

00:23:02.310 --> 00:23:13.240
Now our feelings are becoming one...
Ima bokura no omoi ga hitotsu ni natte

00:23:13.620 --> 00:23:17.290
...and showing the path to us.
michi wo shimesunda

00:23:17.290 --> 00:23:21.560
So please, keep on holding my hand...
Dakara kono te zutto

00:23:21.560 --> 00:23:24.620
...and never let it go...
hanasanaide

00:23:26.030 --> 00:23:27.100
Funadama

00:23:27.100 --> 00:23:28.570
Funadama
Funadama means "soul of the ship," right?

00:23:28.570 --> 00:23:31.810
It turns a boat into a fetish in
order to protect it during a voyage.

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:32.440
Wow!

00:23:32.440 --> 00:23:34.840
It's a bit like our own Astral company badges.

00:23:34.840 --> 00:23:35.940
Oh, is it?

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:38.280
Prof. Miwa has a punishment for you
for not studying enough, Itsuki.

